 		 * linear_metadata; this carries the same contract to an allocator
 		 * that does not consult it. Decode is the RGBX output pool, encode is
 		 * the VDENC direct-RGB source.
+		 *
+		 * CAMERA_WRITE joins them for a different reason with the same remedy
+		 * (bd remora-4ei.9). AOSP's external camera HAL fills every frame with
+		 * the CPU and says so -- ExternalCameraDeviceSession always ORs
+		 * CPU_WRITE_OFTEN | CAMERA_OUTPUT into the stream's producer usage --
+		 * so force_linear above is already true. But a preview buffer is also
+		 * composited, so use_scanout is true as well, and the allocator ranks
+		 * linear_required > SCANOUT > MAPPABLE: scanout wins, NVIDIA hands
+		 * back block-linear, and the HAL then writes linear rows into a tiled
+		 * bo. The result is not subtle -- the written regions read as noise
+		 * and the untouched ones stay zeroed, and a zeroed YUV buffer converts
+		 * to green, which is exactly what a live preview showed.
+		 *
+		 * Scoped to CAMERA_WRITE and not to BO_USE_SW_MASK on purpose:
+		 * promoting every CPU-mapped composited buffer above scanout would
+		 * undo the ranking that venus-nvidia 0023 exists to establish. A
+		 * camera buffer is the narrow case where the producer is unavoidably
+		 * the CPU.
 		 */
-		.linear_required =
-		    (use_flags & (BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER | BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER)) != 0,
+		.linear_required = (use_flags & (BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER | BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER |
